          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            is a good context for doing a lot of category theory (including
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
            theory), but there are some things that are hard to do there, such as to talk about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limits"} weighted limits
            and colimits, and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            theory more generally. This leads one to introduce the notion of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+equipped+with+proarrows"} 2-category equipped with proarrows
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
          %p However, it would also be nice if the extra data in a proarrow equipment were somehow determined by the 2-category we started with. This is especially so when talking about functors between equipments, since functors between 2-categories are often easier to construct. It turns out that in many cases, including the most common ones, this is the case: we can construct the proarrows in terms of the underlying 2-category. This was originally realized by Ross Street.
          %p
            The idea is to identify a profunctor with its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collage"} collage
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cograph+of+a+profunctor"} cograph
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V Cat
            %strong two-sided codiscrete cofibrations
            — i.e. the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+fibration"} two-sided discrete fibrations
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+2-category"} opposite 2-category
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is a 2-category with finite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-colimits"} 2-colimits
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,C\in K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ←
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to B \leftarrow C
            which is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-sided+fibration"} internal two-sided fibration
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{op}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+in+a+2-category"} fibration in a 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Span
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi K
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_{K^{op}}(A,C)
            whose algebras are such fibrations. In other words, there is a
            %em 2-comonad
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Cospan
                    %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cospan_K(A,C)
            whose
            %em coalgebras
            are such fibrations. This 2-comonad is defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ←
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mi A
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A\to B \leftarrow C) \quad \mapsto\quad (A \to (A\times I) +_A B +_C (C\times I) \leftarrow C)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0\to 1)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-\times I)
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} copower
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to A\times I
            is the inclusion at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ×
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C\times I
            is the inclusion at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p
            A cospan
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ←
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to B \leftarrow C
            in a 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is
            %strong codiscrete
            if it is codiscrete in the 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cospan
                      %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cospan_K(A,C)\simeq (A+C)/K
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Cospan
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in Cospan(A,C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cospan
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cospan(A,C)(B,X)
            is equivalent to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \;\rightrightarrows\; X
            of cospans, if there exists a 2-cell from one to the other in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cospan
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cospan(A,C)
          %p
            A
            %strong codiscrete cofibration
            is a two-sided cofibration which is codiscrete as a cospan.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#enriched_categories Enriched categories
          %p
            We sketch a characterization of cofibrations in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is any Bénabou
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos"} cosmos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi g
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\overset{f}{\to} B \overset{g}{\leftarrow} C
            be a cospan and let
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo +
                      %mi A
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo +
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = (A\times I) +_A B +_C (C\times I)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            has the following description.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Its objects are the disjoint union of those of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ob
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi ob
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊔
                        %mi ob
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊔
                        %mi ob
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ob(D) = ob(A) \sqcup ob(B) \sqcup ob(C)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                are (disjoint) full subcategories of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %li
              %p
                There are no morphisms in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
                we have
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi ∅
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(a,b) = D(b,c) = D(a,c) = \emptyset
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(b,a) = B(b,f a)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(c,b) = B(g c, b)
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(c,a) = B(g c, f a)
          %p
            That
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is a
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi i
                  %mi D
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mi j
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \overset{i}{\to} D \overset{j}{\leftarrow} C
            for the inclusions.
          %p
            Now suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a coalgebra for the 2-comonad in question. Therefore, in particular we have a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon B\to D
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cospan
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cospan(A,C)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h f = i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h g = j
            (or perhaps only isomorphic; it really makes no difference here). Moreover, the counit of the comonad is the obvious map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\colon D\to B
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mi h
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k h = 1_B
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            are injective on objects and have disjoint images, so must be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            are fully faithful
            = succeed "-functors," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            on homs must be split monic in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            on homs in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            must be split epic. But since
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h k = 1_B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            on homs must also be split monic, hence an isomorphism, and hence so must that of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            be. Therefore,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            are fully faithful inclusions with disjoint images.
          %p
            Clearly
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            must take the images of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            to the images of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mi h
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k h = 1_B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            takes the rest of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            to itself, sitting in the canonical copy of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            inside
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            satisfies the condition that
          %ul
            %li
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\in C
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∪
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B \setminus (A\cup C)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(a,b) = B(b,c) = B(a,c) = \emptyset
          %p
            It is then easy to check that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            are fully faithful with disjoint images and this condition holds, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is in fact a coalgebra for the comonad in question, i.e. a two-sided cofibration from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Note that such a cofibration from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            can be identified with the following data: a category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B' = B\setminus (A\cup C)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mi ⇸
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\colon A &amp;#8696; B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mi ⇸
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\colon B &amp;#8696; C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mi ⇸
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon A &amp;#8696; C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mi m
                  %mo →
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n m \to p
            of profunctors. Such a thing is sometimes called a
            %strong gamut
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Now a 2-cell in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cospan
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cospan(A,C)
            is simply a natural transformation between functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \;\rightrightarrows\; X
            whose components on the images of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are isomorphisms. Thus, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a cofibration as above with the property that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∪
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \setminus (A\cup C)
            is empty, then it must be codiscrete. The converse is easy to check, taking
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be the ordinal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 4
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4 = (0\le 1 \le 2\le 3)
            as a category. But a gamut with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B'=\emptyset
            is nothing but a profunctor
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mi ⇸
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A &amp;#8696;C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V Cat
            can be precisely identified with the collages of profunctors.
          %h3#toposes Toposes
          %p
            A codiscrete cofibration in the 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Topoi
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topoi
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topoi"} topoi
            can be identified with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact functor
          %h3#double_categories Double categories
          %p
            Codiscrete cofibrations in the 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Dbl
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dbl
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+categories"} double categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+functors"} double functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+transformations"} horizontal transformations
            can be identified with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+profunctors"} double profunctors
          %h2#construction_of_a_proarrow_equipment Construction of a proarrow equipment
          %p
            The examples of profunctors suggest that given any 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            with finite 2-colimits, we may try to canonically equip it with proarrows by defining the proarrows
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mi ⇸
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A &amp;#8696;C
            to be the codiscrete cofibrations. The sticky point is then how to define units and composition of such proarrows in order to obtain an equipment.
          %p
            The unit is obvious: we should take the unit proarrow of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to be the cospan
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %mo ←
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to A\times I \leftarrow A
          %p
            Binary composition is subtler. The obvious way to compose codiscrete cofibrations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ←
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B \leftarrow C
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                    %mo ←
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to D \leftarrow E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo +
                      %mi C
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B +_C D
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              In any 2-category with finite 2-colimits, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              are cofibrations, then so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mo +
                        %mi C
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B +_C D
          %p
            However,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mi C
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B +_C D
            will not be codiscrete even if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            are. In
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            are collages of profunctors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo +
                    %mi C
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B +_C D
            represents the gamut consisting of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n m
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            somehow. The best way to do this seems to be using a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system+on+a+2-category"} factorization system on a 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+relations"} bicategory of relations
            from any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
          %h3#equippable_2categories Equippable 2-categories
          %p
            We are looking for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+system+in+a+2-category"} 2-categorical factorization system
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E},\mathcal{M})
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            such that if we have a two-sided cofibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ←
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to C\leftarrow B
            and we factor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A+B \to C
            into an
            = succeed "-map" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            = succeed "-map," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mo ←
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to E \leftarrow B
            is a codiscrete cofibration. Codiscreteness means in particular that the
            = succeed "-map" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A+B\to E
            should be codiscrete, i.e. representably cofaithful and co-conservative. Moreover, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ←
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to C\leftarrow B
            was already a codiscrete cofibration, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A+B\to C
            should already be in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A 2-category with finite 2-limits and 2-colimits is
              %strong pre-equippable
              if it has a factorization system
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E},\mathcal{M})
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo ←
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to C \leftarrow B
                is a codiscrete cofibration, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo +
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A+B \to C
                is in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              %li
                every morphism in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                is representably co-faithful and co-conservative.
            %p
              It is
              %strong equippable
              if in addition it satisfies:
            %ul
              %li
                Morphisms in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                are closed under pushout and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
                with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
          %p
            Co-conservative morphisms are also called
            = succeed "." do
              %strong liberal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ←
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to C \leftarrow B
            is a codiscrete cofibration, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo +
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A+B\to C
            is cofaithful and liberal; thus the first two conditions are compatible.
          %p
            The example to keep in mind is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is the class of essentially surjective
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            is the class of
            = succeed "-fully-faithful" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Any morphism which is right orthogonal to codiscrete cofibrations is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+morphism"} representably fully faithful
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is pre-equippable, then every morphism in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              is representably fully faithful.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              For any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi I
                      %mo ←
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to X \times I \leftarrow X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo +
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X+X \to X\times I
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Any representably fully faithful morphism is right orthogonal to any
              = succeed "." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  cocomma object
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/cocomma+object"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is pre-equippable and every codiscrete cofibration is a cocomma object, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              is precisely the class of representably fully faithful morphisms.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Maps out of a cocomma object are in canonical correspondence with 2-cells in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is pre-equippable, then any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverter"} inverter
              or
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equifier"} equifier
              is in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is cofaithful and liberal.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p Any inverter is always right orthogonal to any liberal morphism, and any equifier is always right orthogonal to any cofaithful morphism.
          %h3#the_construction The construction
          %p In an equippable 2-category, we can compose cofibrations in the desired way.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is equippable,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                    %mo ←
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to E \leftarrow B
              is a two-sided cofibration, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo +
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A+B \to F \to E
              is an
              = succeed "-factorization," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E},\mathcal{M})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo ←
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to F \leftarrow B
              is a codiscrete cofibration. In particular, the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CodCofib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CodCofib(A,B)
              is coreflective in the category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cofib(A,B)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Since
              = succeed "-morphisms" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo ←
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to F \leftarrow B
              is certainly codiscrete. That it is a cofibration is proven as in (MB, 4.18). Coreflectivity follows by orthogonality for the factorization system
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E},\mathcal{M})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              by assumption.
          %p
            Therefore, in an equippable 2-category, we can define the composite of codiscrete cofibrations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ←
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to B\leftarrow C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                  %mo ←
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to D\leftarrow E
            to be the codiscrete coreflection of the cofibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo +
                      %mi C
                    %mi D
                    %mo ←
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B +_C D\leftarrow E
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is equippable, there is a 2-category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CodCofib
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CodCofib(K)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+fully+faithful+2-functor"} locally fully faithful
              identity-on-objects (pseudo) 2-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi CodCofib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_* K\to CodCofib(K)
              such that each 1-morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
              has a right adjoint. Therefore,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is canonically a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+equipped+with+proarrows"} 2-category equipped with proarrows
              (hence the term “equippable”).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p This is essentially (MB, 4.20).
          %p
            One can then impose additional axioms on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            to get good behavior of this equipment, and try to characterize the equipments arising in this way; see (MB, section 5) and (PC).
          %h3#canonical_factorization_systems Canonical factorization systems
          %p
            Note that since coreflections are determined by a universal property, the composite of codiscrete cofibrations is independent of the chosen factorization system
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E},\mathcal{M})
          %ol
            %li
              Define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              to be the class of liberal and cofaithful morphisms, or
            %li
              Define
